    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1090">

                <pb facs="0957" n="950" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg950"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5123 Manchuria/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-13T16:00:00+08:00">December 13, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 13—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>816. The following telegram has been received from Mukden: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“15, December 10, 4 p.m. An income tax law has been promulgated,
                            effective January 1, and declared applicable to all residents of
                            Manchukuo.</p>
                        <p>Translation follows”.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d1090-f1"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>The Embassy will study the text of the law when received from Mukden.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department, repeated to Tokyo and Embassy, Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
